  "title": "Consciousness routinely misrepresents mental states",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "42342591-979e-48c9-9dd7-b4f78f1c5b19",
      "text": "Inattentively, people are conscious of colors as generic light blue or dark red while their visual states carry specific shades, which attention reveals. So the higher-order awareness routinely misdescribes the states it is about, in a harmless way.",
